<article class="env-definition" id="08EM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08EM">Definition <span data-tag="08EM">36.14.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Consider triples $(T, E, m)$ where </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$T \subset X$ is a closed subset, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$E$ is an object of $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$m \in \mathbf{Z}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> We say <em>approximation holds for the triple</em> $(T, E, m)$ if there exists a perfect object $P$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ supported on $T$ and a map $\alpha : P \to E$ which induces isomorphisms $H^ i(P) \to H^ i(E)$ for $i > m$ and a surjection $H^ m(P) \to H^ m(E)$. </p>
</article>